# Voice Clone

## Authentication

- Browser sign-in uses Cognito hosted UI with Google federation (`auth.<domain>`), PKCE, and `/auth/callback`.
- Runtime Cognito settings come from `config.js` (Terraform writes production `config.js` to the site bucket; local dev uses gitignored `public/config.js` from `public/config.js.example`).
- API calls use Cognito ID tokens in `Authorization: Bearer` headers. API Gateway enforces JWT; Flask verifies JWT again and scopes all voice files to the token email.
- `GET /synthesize` on the internal ALB is the only unauthenticated application route (health check).

## Frontend

- React + Vite + Tailwind. Shared button and layout classes live in `static_site/voice_clone/src/styles/globals.css`.
- No inline styles. One axios client in `src/api/client.js`.

## Backend and data

- No database. Voice inputs and outputs live on the S3 CSI mount under `/mount/<email>/`.
- Do not trust email fields from clients; use the verified JWT email only.

## Architecture diagrams

- Source: `architecture/diagrams/voice-clone.excalidraw`
- Regenerate PNG/SVG: `cd architecture && npm install && npm run export`
- Commit updated exports with infrastructure or auth changes.

## Secrets

- Google OAuth credentials for Cognito: `TF_VAR_cognito_google_client_id` and `TF_VAR_cognito_google_client_secret` at Terraform apply time only.
